   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to increasing the amount of reimbursement the division of veterans' affairs shall provide to local veterans' service agencies for the cost of maintenance of such agencies",
    "basePrintNo": "S6051",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6051-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §359, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6051\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to increasing the\namount of reimbursement the division of veterans' affairs shall\nprovide to local veterans' service agencies for the cost of\nmaintenance of such agencies\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo amend Section 359 of the New York state Executive Law to allow the\nDivision of Veterans' Affairs to fund local veterans service agencies\nat the level of current appropriations.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill amends Section 359 by raising the \"caps\" on funding to local\nveterans service agencies.\n\n EFFECTS OF PRESENT LAW WHICH THIS BILL WOULD ALTER :\nSection 359 of the Executive Law currently provides \"caps\" on funding\nto local veterans service agencies.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe current budget provides funding for aid to local veterans services\nagencies that, if distributed pursuant to existing statute, would\nexceed the \"caps\" currently set forth in section 359 of the executive\nlaw.\n\nThis bill, if enacted, would allow the New York State Division of\nVeterans' Affairs to increase funding to local veterans service\nagencies only to the extent that funding is actually appropriated.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Legislation.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\nThis bill increases the \"caps\" on funding for local veterans service\nagencies but does not mandate increase funding.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to all\nexpenditures made on and after April 1, 2009.\n",
